title: Alcidae
---
# Alcidae

Alcidae is the auk family, holding the guillemots, razorbills, puffins and
auklets of the northern oceans. They are the northern counterpart of the
penguins by convergence rather than descent: the wing drives them after prey
below the surface, but remains just large enough for flight. The compromise is
expensive, and an auk in the air beats its wings almost continuously. Most
species breed in dense colonies on cliffs and lay a single egg on bare rock.
See [[razorbill]].
